## Decompose compose spec into tickets — loop_engine converge loop

**Title:** ${trigger.title}
**Architect spec file:** ${nodes.route-architect.output.spec_file}
**Tech stack:** ${nodes.route-architect.output.tech_stack}
**Testing decisions:** ${nodes.route-architect.output.testing_decisions}
**Reference repos:** ${nodes.route-architect.output.ref_repos}

You are the product-owner. DO NOT implement.

The architect has stamped the spec with a COVERAGE MAP. Each spec story is marked as covered (with WHICH ref repo provides it), partial, or gap. Read the spec file to see the map.

### Call loop_engine

Call `loop_engine` with:

- `goal`: "Decompose compose spec into ticket plan: ${trigger.title}"
- `runner`: "product-owner"
- `max_iterations`: 3

- `execution`: {
    title: "[plan-exec] Decompose compose spec into ticket plan",
    body: "Read the stamped spec file at ${nodes.route-architect.output.spec_file}. It has a Coverage Map. Each story lists a Source (which ref repo covers it) and ref location. Create a TICKET PLAN with two types of tickets:\n\n**PORT tickets** (for covered/partial stories): Title format `[ticket-NN] Port from <ref-name>: <story>`. Body must include: the ref repo path, the specific ref file(s) to port, what to adapt (language differences, API changes, conventions), and acceptance criteria from the spec.\n\n**BUILD tickets** (for gap stories — integration layer, new features): Title format `[ticket-NN] <story>`. Body must include: acceptance criteria from the spec, what it integrates, and tech stack. No ref implementation exists.\n\nFor each ticket include: title, what-to-build, blocked-by (dependency numbers), ticket_type (port|build), and source_ref (which ref repo, or null for build tickets). Output the complete ticket plan.",
    assignee: "product-owner",
    skill: "to-tickets"
  }

- `verifier`: {
    title: "[plan-review] Review compose ticket plan",
    body: "Review the ticket plan against the spec file at ${nodes.route-architect.output.spec_file}. Check:\n\n1. COVERAGE: Does every spec story have a ticket?\n2. PORT ACCURACY: Do port tickets reference the correct ref repo and files from the coverage map?\n3. INTEGRATION: Are there BUILD tickets for the integration gaps that connect the ported components?\n4. DEPENDENCIES: Are dependencies correct? Port tickets should come before integration tickets.\n\nVerdict: advance (plan is good) or replan (list specific gaps).",
    assignee: "verifier",
    metric_type: "ground_truth"
  }

After convergence, create the ticket cards via `kanban_create`. Two types:\n\n**Port tickets**: `title: "[ticket-NN] Port from <ref-name>: <story>"`, `assignee: "tech-lead"`, body includes ref repo path + ref file path + adaptation notes + acceptance criteria.\n**Build tickets**: `title: "[ticket-NN] <story>"`, `assignee: "tech-lead"`, body includes acceptance criteria + what it integrates + tech stack.\n\nEach ticket fires tech-lead-execute independently when tech-lead completes it.

### Complete with metadata

```
{decomposed: true, ticket_count: N, ticket_ids: ["<id1>", ...], port_tickets: N, build_tickets: N}
```
